  catalytic         2.7687       0.1301            0.88
       hill         1.5792       0.5038            3.39
  (upstream rail width sigma = sqrt(V/Omega) = 0.4727 at Omega = 30)
  **A cascade needs the downstream to survive ordinary upstream fluctuation.**
  A margin of a few sigma is a noise margin; a fraction of a sigma is not.
  -> P1(a) HOLDS for both schemes
  -> P1(b) source DOES NOT TRANSMIT;  catalytic transmits
  -> only ['catalytic', 'hill'] can be called a cascade. The other is measured anyway, as the control that shows what a non-transmitting chain looks like.

